    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jackson Merrill** headlining the offensive unit. His score of 75.27 is our highest of the day, bolstered by a favorable matchup against Trey Yesavage (4.55 xERA) and an ideal batting order slot. We also see high-end production potential from **Gunnar Henderson** (69.90) and **Kyle Tucker** (69.76). While **Gunnar Henderson** faces a slight negative platoon adjustment against Noah Cameron, his elite floor and order position make him a core start. **Andy Pages** (65.76) earns a strong recommendation due to the secondary benefit of a slow-delivering pitcher in Brandon Pfaadt, which creates an advantageous environment for his stolen base potential\u2014a critical factor given the scarcity of speed in our league.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today\u2019s lineup involved the utility and bench spots. **Miguel Vargas** (52.70) was the primary candidate for entry, nearly displacing our lower-scoring starters, but was ultimately left on the bench. While his xwOBA of 0.398 is impressive, the optimizer favored the higher raw projections and positional flexibility provided by the active starters. We are keeping a close watch on **Jorge Polanco**, who remains a marginal start (52.15); while he is currently active, a 45% rain risk creates significant volatility. Should that game be postponed, we have the flexibility to pivot, though we must navigate these game caps carefully to avoid squandering remaining utility slots. With **Drake Baldwin** and **Liam Hicks** still pending official lineup confirmation, the Austin Waves remain poised to adjust should any late-scratch updates materialize.",
